/* GENERATED from the games' own rulesButton sections — regenerate when any game's rules change (see CLAUDE.md). */
window.RULES_DATA={"backgammon":{"title":"Backgammon","sections":[{"h":"Goal","t":"March all 15 of your checkers around the board into your home quarter, then bear them off. First player to bear off every checker wins."},{"h":"Your turn","t":"Roll two dice — each die is a separate move (one checker twice, or two checkers once each). Doubles play FOUR times. Checkers move toward your home; the highlights show every legal landing."},{"h":"Points & blots","t":"Two or more of your checkers on a point OWN it — opponents can't land there. A lone checker is a BLOT: an enemy landing on it sends it to the bar in the middle.","ex":"Building a wall of owned points in front of their runners (a “prime”) can trap checkers for the whole midgame."},{"h":"The bar","t":"A checker on the bar must re-enter in the OPPONENT'S home quarter before you may move anything else — dice that can't enter are wasted. Against a strong home board, a hit can cost several full turns."},{"h":"Bearing off","t":"Once ALL your checkers reach your home quarter, dice remove them: a 5 bears off a checker from the 5-point. A roll higher than your highest occupied point may bear off from the highest. Get hit during bear-off and that checker travels the whole board again."},{"h":"The doubling cube","t":"Feeling ahead? Offer the cube to double the stakes BEFORE rolling. Your opponent either resigns the game at the current stake or accepts — and then only THEY may double next. The cube turns good positions into hard decisions.","ex":"You're up but one lucky hit could flip it. Doubling now forces them to pay to find out."},{"h":"Gammons","t":"Win before your opponent bears off a single checker and it's a GAMMON — double value. If they also have a checker on the bar or in your home, BACKGAMMON — triple. The stats remember."}]},"battleship":{"title":"Battleship","sections":[{"h":"Goal","t":"Sink the enemy's entire fleet of five ships before they sink yours."},{"h":"The fleet","t":"Carrier (5 squares), Battleship (4), Cruiser (3), Submarine (3), Destroyer (2). Each hides somewhere on a 10×10 grid — straight lines only, no overlaps. Shuffle deals you random layouts until one feels lucky, then Lock it in. The pass curtain keeps fleets secret."},{"h":"Firing","t":"On your turn, tap a square on the enemy grid. A HIT marks red, a MISS marks white — then the phone passes. Your own grid below shows the shots they've taken at you."},{"h":"Hunting","svg":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 280 76\"><g><rect x=\"36\" y=\"8\" width=\"22\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#15375a\"/><rect x=\"62\" y=\"8\" width=\"22\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#15375a\"/><rect x=\"88\" y=\"8\" width=\"22\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#15375a\"/><rect x=\"114\" y=\"8\" width=\"22\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#15375a\"/><rect x=\"140\" y=\"8\" width=\"22\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#15375a\"/><rect x=\"166\" y=\"8\" width=\"22\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#15375a\"/><rect x=\"192\" y=\"8\" width=\"22\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#15375a\"/><rect x=\"218\" y=\"8\" width=\"22\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#15375a\"/><rect x=\"36\" y=\"30\" width=\"22\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#15375a\"/><rect x=\"62\" y=\"30\" width=\"22\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#15375a\"/><rect x=\"88\" y=\"30\" width=\"22\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#15375a\"/><rect x=\"114\" y=\"30\" width=\"22\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#15375a\"/><rect x=\"140\" y=\"30\" width=\"22\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#15375a\"/><rect x=\"166\" y=\"30\" width=\"22\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#15375a\"/><rect x=\"192\" y=\"30\" width=\"22\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#15375a\"/><rect x=\"218\" y=\"30\" width=\"22\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#15375a\"/><rect x=\"36\" y=\"52\" width=\"22\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#15375a\"/><rect x=\"62\" y=\"52\" width=\"22\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#15375a\"/><rect x=\"88\" y=\"52\" width=\"22\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#15375a\"/><rect x=\"114\" y=\"52\" width=\"22\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#15375a\"/><rect x=\"140\" y=\"52\" width=\"22\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#15375a\"/><rect x=\"166\" y=\"52\" width=\"22\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#15375a\"/><rect x=\"192\" y=\"52\" width=\"22\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#15375a\"/><rect x=\"218\" y=\"52\" width=\"22\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#15375a\"/><circle cx=\"125\" cy=\"39\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#d8312b\"/><circle cx=\"99\" cy=\"39\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f4c542\"/><circle cx=\"151\" cy=\"39\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f4c542\"/><circle cx=\"125\" cy=\"17\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f4c542\"/><circle cx=\"125\" cy=\"61\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f4c542\"/><text x=\"232\" y=\"42\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#9cb8cc\" font-family=\"system-ui\">hit? try the</text><text x=\"232\" y=\"55\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#9cb8cc\" font-family=\"system-ui\">4 neighbors</text></g></svg>","t":"Until you hit, fire a spread — checkerboard patterns find every ship (nothing is smaller than 2). After a hit, probe the four neighbors to find the ship's direction, then walk the line until she sinks.","ex":"Hit at E5. E6 misses, E4 hits — she runs vertical. E3… E2… “You sank my Battleship!”"},{"h":"Sinking","t":"When every square of a ship is hit, the game announces the sinking — and which ship it was. That's free intel: sank the Destroyer? Nothing left is shorter than 3, so widen your search pattern."},{"h":"Victory","t":"All seventeen enemy squares found wins the war. The stats track your accuracy — the family sharpshooter title is forever."}]},"bridge":{"title":"Bridge Builders","sections":[{"h":"Goal","t":"It's a race: build a connected bridge of words from your ▶ arrow on the left edge all the way to the right edge of the board."},{"h":"The board","svg":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 280 110\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"6\" width=\"268\" height=\"98\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#143540\"/><polygon points=\"12,30 24,37 12,44\" fill=\"#d8312b\"/><polygon points=\"12,66 24,73 12,80\" fill=\"#2f6fd0\"/><g font-family=\"system-ui\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"800\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><rect x=\"30\" y=\"28\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f2e4bf\"/><text x=\"39\" y=\"41\" fill=\"#143540\">W</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"28\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f2e4bf\"/><text x=\"59\" y=\"41\" fill=\"#143540\">E</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"48\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f2e4bf\"/><text x=\"59\" y=\"61\" fill=\"#143540\">B</text><rect x=\"46\" y=\"48\" width=\"0\" height=\"0\"/></g><line x1=\"78\" y1=\"55\" x2=\"240\" y2=\"55\" stroke=\"#9fc\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/><polygon points=\"240,48 254,55 240,62\" fill=\"#9fc\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"46\" fill=\"#9fc\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"system-ui\">build word by word →</text></svg>","t":"Two arrows sit on the left edge, one in each player's color. Your first word must cover YOUR arrow. From there, every play grows your bridge toward the right side."},{"h":"Your tiles are yours","t":"Every tile is ringed in the color of whoever played it. Each new play must build off your OWN tiles: at least one word you form this turn must contain a tile you already own on the board."},{"h":"Spelling through the enemy","t":"You may spell straight through the other player's letters — their tiles count for the word and its score — but they NEVER count as part of your bridge. Only your own colored tiles connect.","ex":"Your L sits on the board, their I sits right after it. You play N, T, S to make L-I-N-T-S: a legal word, full points — but for crossing purposes your bridge has a gap where their I is."},{"h":"Scoring & the shuffled bonuses","t":"Words score like Scrabble: letter values, DL/TL boost a letter, DW/TW boost the word (first cover only), +50 for all 7 tiles. The twist: the bonus squares keep their positions but their TYPES reshuffle every game — scout the board before you plan your route!"},{"h":"Crossing","t":"The moment one of your own tiles lands in the rightmost column, the game ends at the end of that turn, and you bank a +10 crossing bonus."},{"h":"The bridge bonus","t":"Then each player's bridge is traced for its best continuous path from the left edge: every word along the path scores its full value once, and vertical connector letters add their points where the path climbs through them. Both bridge bonuses are added to the turn scores — highest grand total wins, so a rich, connected bridge can beat a fast, skinny one!","ex":"You crossed first (+10) with a thin bridge worth 31. They never crossed, but their fat bridge traces to 58 — if their turn score is close to yours, they can still win on totals."}]},"checkers":{"title":"Checkers","sections":[{"h":"Goal","t":"Capture or trap every enemy piece. You win when your opponent has no pieces left — or no legal move."},{"h":"Moving","t":"Pieces slide one square diagonally, forward only, onto an empty dark square. Tap your piece to see its moves glow, then tap where to go."},{"h":"Jumping","svg":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 280 90\"><g><rect x=\"40\" y=\"10\" width=\"66\" height=\"66\" fill=\"#7a4a26\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"106\" y=\"10\" width=\"66\" height=\"66\" fill=\"#caa97a\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"172\" y=\"10\" width=\"66\" height=\"66\" fill=\"#7a4a26\" rx=\"4\"/><circle cx=\"73\" cy=\"43\" r=\"20\" fill=\"#2f6fd0\"/><circle cx=\"139\" cy=\"43\" r=\"20\" fill=\"#d8312b\"/><path d=\"M73 18 Q139 -14 205 18\" stroke=\"#f4c542\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"199,8 212,20 196,22\" fill=\"#f4c542\"/><line x1=\"124\" y1=\"28\" x2=\"154\" y2=\"58\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><line x1=\"154\" y1=\"28\" x2=\"124\" y2=\"58\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g></svg>","t":"If an enemy piece sits diagonally next to you with an empty square right behind it, you JUMP it — hop over and it's captured off the board."},{"h":"Captures are forced","t":"If any of your pieces can jump, you MUST jump — you can choose which jump, but you can't make a quiet move instead. The message bar warns you: “must capture.”","ex":"You'd love to push your back-row piece forward, but one of your pieces has a jump available. The board only highlights the jumping piece — take the capture."},{"h":"Chain jumps","t":"If your jumping piece lands where it can jump AGAIN, it must keep going — one turn can clear two, three, even more pieces. The chain ends when no more jumps are available from that piece."},{"h":"Kings","t":"Reach the far row and your piece is crowned a King. Kings move and jump diagonally in ALL four directions. If a piece is crowned mid-jump, the chain ends there — coronation first, conquest later."},{"h":"vs Computer","t":"Easy blunders generously, Medium plays a solid game, Hard searches ahead and will punish loose pieces. The computer takes the second seat."}]},"chess":{"title":"Chess","sections":[{"h":"Goal","t":"Checkmate the enemy king — attack it so it cannot escape. The board lights every legal move when you pick a piece up, so you can learn by looking."},{"h":"How the pieces move","t":"Pawns step forward one (two from home), capture diagonally. Knights jump in an L — the only piece that leaps over others. Bishops run diagonals; rooks run ranks and files; the queen does both. The king steps one square any direction."},{"h":"Check & checkmate","t":"When your king is attacked, you're in CHECK (the king glows red) and must fix it immediately — move the king, block, or capture the attacker. If nothing fixes it: checkmate, game over.","ex":"A back-rank mate: their rook slides to your home rank, your king is fenced in by its own pawns — no escape, no block. The oldest trick in the book."},{"h":"Castling","svg":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 280 70\"><g font-size=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><rect x=\"40\" y=\"14\" width=\"200\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#1c2b22\"/><text x=\"65\" y=\"44\">♔</text><text x=\"215\" y=\"44\">♖</text><path d=\"M88 26 Q140 6 192 26\" stroke=\"#f4c542\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/><polygon points=\"186,18 196,26 182,30\" fill=\"#f4c542\"/><path d=\"M192 50 Q150 64 110 50\" stroke=\"#9fc\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/><polygon points=\"116,58 106,50 120,44\" fill=\"#9fc\"/></g></svg>","t":"Once per game your king may slide TWO squares toward a rook, and the rook hops to the far side — king to safety, rook to the fight. Allowed only if neither piece has moved, the path is clear, and the king isn't in check or crossing an attacked square. Tap the king two squares sideways to do it."},{"h":"En passant","t":"If an enemy pawn double-steps and lands exactly beside your pawn, you may capture it AS IF it had moved one square — but only on the very next move. The board offers it when it's legal; it surprises everyone the first time.","ex":"Your pawn stands on the 5th rank. Their pawn jumps two squares, landing beside you — take it diagonally behind, and it's off the board."},{"h":"Promotion","t":"A pawn reaching the far rank becomes any piece you like — almost always a queen, but the picker offers knight, rook, and bishop for the rare position that wants them."},{"h":"Draws","t":"Stalemate (no legal moves, but not in check), threefold repetition, fifty quiet moves, or bare-bones material — the game calls these automatically."},{"h":"vs Computer: levels 1–10","t":"Level 1 barely looks ahead and blunders generously — perfect while learning. Each level climbs in real strength: 5–6 gives a casual adult a fight, 8+ plays serious club-level chess. The shelf remembers your level."},{"h":"🎓 Coach","t":"Coach mode adds three helpers: HINT shows a strong move and says why in plain words, the BLUNDER NUDGE taps your shoulder before a move that loses material (you can still play it — your game!), and TAKEBACK undoes your last move so mistakes become lessons. Climb a level when the coach gets quiet."}]},"chinese":{"title":"Chinese Checkers","sections":[{"h":"Goal","t":"Race all ten of your marbles across the star into the opposite point. First full destination triangle wins."},{"h":"Your turn","t":"Move ONE marble: either a single step to an adjacent hole, or a HOP over any one adjacent marble (yours or theirs) into the empty hole directly beyond."},{"h":"Hop chains","t":"Hops CHAIN: after one hop, the same marble may keep hopping as long as landings exist — a well-built ladder can carry a marble across the whole board in one breathtaking turn. Tap your marble and the board lights every reachable hole, chains included.","ex":"Marbles spaced gap-by-gap form a highway: hop-hop-hop-hop — one move, half the board. Both players can ride a ladder, so build the on-ramp on YOUR side."},{"h":"No captures","t":"Nothing is ever removed — hopped marbles are stepping stones, not victims. The whole game is geometry: build ladders for yourself that arrive a tempo too late for them."},{"h":"Don't strand the stragglers","t":"The classic loss: nine marbles home, one lonely marble three turns behind with no one left to hop. Keep the group loosely together — the last marble's trip matters as much as the first's."}]},"codebreaker":{"title":"Codebreaker","sections":[{"h":"Goal","t":"One player sets a secret 4-peg color code; the other has 10 guesses to crack it. Then you swap — fewer guesses wins."},{"h":"Setting the code","t":"The setter secretly picks 4 pegs from 6 colors — repeats ARE allowed, and doubles make wickedly harder codes. The pass curtain keeps it hidden."},{"h":"The clues","svg":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 280 60\"><g><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"30\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#d8312b\"/><circle cx=\"72\" cy=\"30\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#f4c542\"/><circle cx=\"104\" cy=\"30\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#46b06a\"/><circle cx=\"136\" cy=\"30\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#2f6fd0\"/><rect x=\"168\" y=\"12\" width=\"100\" height=\"36\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1c2b22\"/><circle cx=\"186\" cy=\"24\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#111\"/><circle cx=\"204\" cy=\"24\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#111\"/><circle cx=\"222\" cy=\"24\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#fff\"/><text x=\"218\" y=\"46\" font-size=\"9.5\" fill=\"#cfe6d8\" font-family=\"system-ui\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2 black · 1 white</text></g></svg>","t":"After each guess: a BLACK clue peg for every guess peg that's the right color in the right spot, a WHITE peg for right color, wrong spot. The clue pegs are NOT in order — they describe the guess as a whole.","ex":"Code R-Y-G-B, guess R-G-Y-Y: the R earns a black; G and Y are present but misplaced — two whites. The second Y earns nothing: clues never count a code peg twice."},{"h":"Cracking it","t":"Early guesses should SPREAD colors to learn what's in the code; later guesses rearrange what you know. Every clue rules out thousands of codes — write nothing down, argue everything out loud."},{"h":"The duel","t":"Both players set and both players guess — the cracker who needed fewer guesses takes the game. A code unbroken in 10 scores as 11 against you, so setters: be cruel."}]},"connect4":{"title":"Connect 4","sections":[{"h":"Goal","t":"Be first to line up FOUR of your discs in a row — across, down, or diagonally."},{"h":"Your turn","t":"Tap a column and your disc drops to the lowest empty slot. Gravity is the whole game: you can only ever land on top of the stack."},{"h":"The diagonal sneak","svg":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 280 96\"><rect x=\"60\" y=\"6\" width=\"160\" height=\"84\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#2f4f8a\"/><g><circle cx=\"76\" cy=\"20\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#16223c\"/><circle cx=\"98\" cy=\"20\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#16223c\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"20\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#16223c\"/><circle cx=\"142\" cy=\"20\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#16223c\"/><circle cx=\"164\" cy=\"20\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#d8312b\"/><circle cx=\"186\" cy=\"20\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#16223c\"/><circle cx=\"208\" cy=\"20\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#16223c\"/><circle cx=\"76\" cy=\"40\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#16223c\"/><circle cx=\"98\" cy=\"40\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#16223c\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"40\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#16223c\"/><circle cx=\"142\" cy=\"40\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#d8312b\"/><circle cx=\"164\" cy=\"40\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#16223c\"/><circle cx=\"186\" cy=\"40\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#16223c\"/><circle cx=\"208\" cy=\"40\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#16223c\"/><circle cx=\"76\" cy=\"60\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#16223c\"/><circle cx=\"98\" cy=\"60\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#16223c\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"60\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#d8312b\"/><circle cx=\"142\" cy=\"60\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#f4c542\"/><circle cx=\"164\" cy=\"60\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#f4c542\"/><circle cx=\"186\" cy=\"60\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#16223c\"/><circle cx=\"208\" cy=\"60\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#16223c\"/><circle cx=\"76\" cy=\"80\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#f4c542\"/><circle cx=\"98\" cy=\"80\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#d8312b\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"80\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#f4c542\"/><circle cx=\"142\" cy=\"80\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#f4c542\"/><circle cx=\"164\" cy=\"80\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#f4c542\"/><circle cx=\"186\" cy=\"80\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#16223c\"/><circle cx=\"208\" cy=\"80\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#16223c\"/></g></svg>","t":"Horizontal and vertical threats are easy to spot. Diagonals win games — they build quietly out of moves that each looked innocent.","ex":"Red's discs at different heights in four neighboring columns suddenly line up corner-to-corner. Yellow never saw it — nobody ever does."},{"h":"Double threats","t":"The strongest move creates TWO ways to win at once — your opponent can only block one. If you must defend, block the line that's already three long first."},{"h":"Draws","t":"Fill all 42 slots with no four-in-a-row and it's a draw. Rare — someone usually cracks first."}]},"dominoes":{"title":"Dominoes","sections":[{"h":"Goal","t":"Be first to play every tile in your hand — or be caught holding the fewest pips when the game blocks."},{"h":"Setup & the line","t":"Each player draws 7 tiles. Tiles join end-to-end: a tile may be played only where its number MATCHES the open end of the line. Doubles sit crosswise.","ex":"The line's open ends show 3 and 5. Your 5-2 plays on the 5 end — now the ends are 3 and 2."},{"h":"Can't play?","t":"Draw from the boneyard until you CAN play. If the boneyard is empty and you still can't move, you pass."},{"h":"Going out & blocking","t":"Play your last tile — “domino!” — and you win the hand. If NOBODY can play and the boneyard's dry, the hand is blocked: lowest pip total in hand wins it."},{"h":"Reading the bones","t":"There are seven of each number in the set. Count what's on the table: if five 6s are down and you hold the sixth, only one 6 remains anywhere — steering the line toward numbers you control is how sharks play.","ex":"You hold 6-4 and 6-1, and four 6s are already on the table. Force a 6 end and odds are they'll be drawing."}]},"dots":{"title":"Dots & Boxes","sections":[{"h":"Goal","t":"Claim more boxes than your opponent. A box is yours when you draw its FOURTH side — it fills with your color."},{"h":"Your turn","t":"Tap between two neighboring dots to draw one line. Complete a box and you claim it AND move again — chain completions as long as they last."},{"h":"Don't give the third side","t":"Early game is a dance of NOT drawing the third side of any box — the third side is a gift. Count before you draw.","ex":"Only “safe” lines remain that all create a third side somewhere. Whoever runs out of safe moves first opens the floodgates."},{"h":"Chains","t":"Late game, boxes form chains — open one and your opponent eats the WHOLE chain. The trick is to open the SHORTEST chain available, feeding them little to save the big chains for yourself."},{"h":"The double-cross","t":"The expert move: when gobbling a long chain, leave the LAST TWO boxes by drawing the closing line instead. You sacrifice two boxes — but your opponent must open the next chain for you. Whoever controls the chain count usually controls the game.","ex":"A 7-chain and a 5-chain remain. Take 5 of the 7, decline the last two — they get 2, then must hand you the 5-chain. You: 10, them: 2."}]},"farkle":{"title":"Farkle","sections":[{"h":"Goal","t":"First to 5,000 points. But every roll you push your luck, you're gambling the whole turn."},{"h":"Your turn","t":"Roll six dice. Set aside at least one SCORING die or combo, then either bank your turn total or re-roll the rest. Use all six and they come back — hot dice! — and the turn keeps building."},{"h":"Scoring","t":"Single 1 = 100. Single 5 = 50. Three of a kind = 100× the number (three 2s = 200… three 6s = 600) except three 1s = 1,000. Four/five/six of a kind double each step. A 1–6 straight and three pairs score too — the picker only lets you select legal combos, and the running total shows what your selection is worth.","ex":"You roll 1,1,5,3,3,6: take both 1s and the 5 (250) and roll three dice — or take just one 1 (100) and roll five for better odds at trips."},{"h":"FARKLE!","t":"Roll and score NOTHING — that's a Farkle: your entire unbanked turn total vanishes and play passes. The deeper the run, the harder the fall. Three pairs on the opening six saves you; two dead dice late won't."},{"h":"The opening rule","t":"The Open/500 button picks your house rule: “Open” lets anyone bank any amount; “500” means you can't bank your FIRST points of the game until a single turn reaches 500 — the classic high-pressure start."},{"h":"Banking wisdom","t":"One or two dice left is the danger zone — roughly a coin flip to Farkle on two, worse on one. Banking 300 beats explaining how you lost 1,200.","ex":"Turn total 850 with two dice in hand. Bank it. Yes, even though hot dice would feel amazing. BANK it."}]},"gofish":{"title":"Go Fish","sections":[{"h":"Goal","t":"Collect the most BOOKS — all four cards of one rank. Thirteen books exist; majority wins."},{"h":"Your turn","t":"Ask the other player for a rank you ALREADY hold at least one of: “Got any Sevens?” If they do, they hand over ALL of them — and you ASK AGAIN. Keep hitting, keep asking."},{"h":"Go fish!","t":"If they have none, they say “Go fish!” and you draw one card. Draw the very rank you asked for? Show it — and your turn continues! Otherwise the turn passes."},{"h":"Books","t":"The moment you hold all four of a rank, the book banks automatically and scores. Your hand groups cards by rank so near-books are easy to spot."},{"h":"Memory is the game","t":"Every ask is information — theirs AND yours. If they asked for Queens two turns ago, they still hold Queens… unless you fished one since.","ex":"They asked for Nines, then drew twice. You just picked up a Nine — asking for Nines now likely nets you theirs AND another turn."},{"h":"Empty hands","t":"Out of cards mid-game? Draw from the pond and play on. The game ends when all 13 books are made — most books takes it."}]},"gomoku":{"title":"Gomoku","sections":[{"h":"Goal","t":"Place stones on the intersections and be first to get FIVE in a row — across, down, or diagonally."},{"h":"Your turn","t":"Tap any empty point to place a stone. Stones never move and are never captured — the board only fills."},{"h":"Open threats","t":"An open three (three in a row with BOTH ends free) must be answered immediately — ignored, it becomes an open four, which is unstoppable: two winning ends, one blocker.","ex":"You spot their ·XXX· — block an end NOW. If you see ·XXXX· it's already over."},{"h":"The double threat","t":"The classic win is making two open threes with a single stone — a fork. Your opponent blocks one, you complete the other. Building quiet crossing shapes beats racing in a straight line."},{"h":"First-move advantage","t":"Going first is a real edge — the coin flip matters. House etiquette: alternate who starts across games (your stats track who went first)."}]},"guesswho":{"title":"Guess Who","sections":[{"h":"Goal","t":"Figure out which character the other player is before they figure out who YOU are."},{"h":"Setup","t":"Each player secretly taps the character they ARE — the pass screen keeps it private. Don't let them see!"},{"h":"Your turn","t":"Ask the other player ONE yes/no question out loud — the app doesn't referee, you two do. They must answer honestly about their character. Then flip down everyone you've ruled out and tap Done — pass.","ex":"“Do you wear glasses?” — “No.” Tap all 8 glasses-wearers to flip them face-down. 16 suspects left."},{"h":"Your flips are yours","svg":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 280 84\"><g font-family=\"system-ui\"><rect x=\"20\" y=\"8\" width=\"52\" height=\"66\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fdf6e9\"/><circle cx=\"46\" cy=\"32\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#d9a06b\"/><circle cx=\"41\" cy=\"30\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#222\"/><circle cx=\"51\" cy=\"30\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#222\"/><path d=\"M40 40 Q46 45 52 40\" stroke=\"#8d3a3a\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><text x=\"46\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#4a3340\" font-weight=\"700\">up</text><rect x=\"92\" y=\"8\" width=\"52\" height=\"66\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#7c2f43\"/><text x=\"118\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"28\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.4)\" font-weight=\"900\">?</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"36\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#e2ccd5\">face-down =</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#e2ccd5\">ruled out</text></g></svg>","t":"Each player has their OWN board of flips. When the phone passes, your flips come back exactly as you left them — and the pass screen whispers who you are, so you can answer their questions truthfully."},{"h":"Making a guess","t":"Think you've got them? Tap Make a guess, then tap the character, then tap them AGAIN to lock it in. Right: you win on the spot. Wrong: you LOSE on the spot — classic rules, so be sure!","ex":"4 suspects left but you're feeling lucky? A wrong guess hands them the game. One more question is usually cheaper."},{"h":"Fair questions","t":"Any yes/no question about how the character LOOKS is fair: hair color, hat, glasses, beard, earrings, smile. “Does your name start with M?” is legal in house rules — you two decide!"}]},"hex":{"title":"Hex","sections":[{"h":"Goal","t":"Connect your two sides of the board with an unbroken chain of your stones. One player connects top to bottom, the other left to right — the colored edges show whose is whose."},{"h":"Your turn","t":"Tap any empty hex to claim it. Stones never move and are never captured. That's the whole rulebook — the depth comes free."},{"h":"No draws. Ever.","t":"A completely filled Hex board ALWAYS contains exactly one winning connection — it's mathematically impossible to draw. To block your opponent is to build your own wall: defense IS offense."},{"h":"Bridges","svg":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 280 80\"><g><polygon points=\"70,40 80,23 100,23 110,40 100,57 80,57\" fill=\"#d8312b\"/><polygon points=\"150,12 160,-5 180,-5 190,12 180,29 160,29\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"130,8 140,-9 160,-9 170,8 160,25 140,25\" fill=\"#d8312b\" transform=\"translate(20,16)\"/><polygon points=\"110,40 120,23 140,23 150,40 140,57 120,57\" fill=\"#1c2b22\" stroke=\"#3a5a47\"/><polygon points=\"130,72 140,55 160,55 170,72 160,89 140,89\" fill=\"#1c2b22\" stroke=\"#3a5a47\" transform=\"translate(0,-16)\"/><text x=\"196\" y=\"46\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#cfe6d8\" font-family=\"system-ui\">two ways across =</text><text x=\"196\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#cfe6d8\" font-family=\"system-ui\">unbreakable link</text></g></svg>","t":"Two of your stones placed diagonally with TWO shared empty neighbors form a bridge: if your opponent takes one connector, you take the other. Bridges let you leap across the board in half the moves — connect the bridges last."},{"h":"Edge play","t":"Stones near your own edges connect to them in multiple ways — don't hug the edge too early. The center is the strongest opening area; corner-ish first moves are weak."}]},"mancala":{"title":"Mancala","sections":[{"h":"Goal","t":"Bank more stones in your store (the big bowl on your right) than your opponent banks in theirs."},{"h":"Sowing","svg":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 280 70\"><rect x=\"8\" y=\"14\" width=\"34\" height=\"42\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#5a3f24\"/><rect x=\"238\" y=\"14\" width=\"34\" height=\"42\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#5a3f24\"/><g><circle cx=\"64\" cy=\"48\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#7a5c38\"/><circle cx=\"64\" cy=\"22\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#7a5c38\"/><circle cx=\"94\" cy=\"48\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#7a5c38\"/><circle cx=\"94\" cy=\"22\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#7a5c38\"/><circle cx=\"124\" cy=\"48\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#7a5c38\"/><circle cx=\"124\" cy=\"22\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#7a5c38\"/><circle cx=\"154\" cy=\"48\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#7a5c38\"/><circle cx=\"154\" cy=\"22\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#7a5c38\"/><circle cx=\"184\" cy=\"48\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#7a5c38\"/><circle cx=\"184\" cy=\"22\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#7a5c38\"/><circle cx=\"214\" cy=\"48\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#7a5c38\"/><circle cx=\"214\" cy=\"22\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#7a5c38\"/><path d=\"M94 60 Q140 76 214 56 Q244 48 250 38\" stroke=\"#f4c542\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/><polygon points=\"244,32 254,36 246,44\" fill=\"#f4c542\"/></g></svg>","t":"Tap one of YOUR six pits: scoop up all its stones and sow them one per pit counter-clockwise — dropping into your own store as you pass it, but always SKIPPING your opponent's store."},{"h":"Free turn","t":"If your LAST stone lands exactly in your store, you go again. Chaining free turns is the heart of the game — the opening that lands in your store on move one is famous for a reason.","ex":"Your third pit holds exactly 3 stones — the last one drops in your store. Free turn. Now look for the next one."},{"h":"The capture","t":"If your last stone lands in an EMPTY pit on YOUR side, you capture that stone PLUS every stone in the opposite pit — all of it into your store. Watch your opponent's big pits and time the raid.","ex":"Their pit across from your empty one holds 7. Land your last stone in that empty pit: 8 stones swing to your store at once."},{"h":"Game end","t":"When one side's six pits are all empty, the game ends — and the OTHER player sweeps every stone left on their side into their store. Sometimes starving your own side is the winning endgame. Most stones wins."}]},"morris":{"title":"Nine Men's Morris","sections":[{"h":"Goal","t":"Reduce your opponent to two pieces — or freeze them with no legal move."},{"h":"Three phases","t":"PLACING: take turns putting your nine pieces on empty points. MOVING: slide pieces along lines to adjacent points. FLYING: down to exactly three pieces, yours may jump to ANY empty point — desperation grants wings."},{"h":"Mills","svg":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 280 64\"><line x1=\"60\" y1=\"32\" x2=\"220\" y2=\"32\" stroke=\"#caa97a\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"60\" cy=\"32\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#d8312b\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"32\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#d8312b\"/><circle cx=\"220\" cy=\"32\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#d8312b\"/><circle cx=\"60\" cy=\"32\" r=\"17\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#f4c542\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"32\" r=\"17\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#f4c542\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"220\" cy=\"32\" r=\"17\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#f4c542\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></svg>","t":"Three of your pieces in a straight line ALONG A DRAWN LINE is a mill — form one and you immediately remove an enemy piece of your choice. Pieces inside enemy mills are protected unless nothing else is available."},{"h":"Swinging mills","t":"The killer pattern: two mills sharing a corner, opened and re-closed each turn, grinding a capture every single move. Build toward shapes that can swing; break your opponent's before they finish.","ex":"Slide a piece OUT of your mill this turn, slide it BACK next turn — mill re-formed, another piece taken. Repeat until they concede or run dry."},{"h":"Placement is destiny","t":"The crossing points (where three or four lines meet) are the strong squares. A cramped placement phase loses the moving phase before it starts — spread, threaten two mills at once, and make every block they play cost them shape."}]},"reversi":{"title":"Reversi","sections":[{"h":"Goal","t":"Finish with more discs of your color showing. Every disc can flip many times — the only count that matters is the last one."},{"h":"Flanking","svg":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 280 64\"><g><rect x=\"33\" y=\"12\" width=\"34\" height=\"34\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#1c3a28\"/><circle cx=\"50\" cy=\"29\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#e8e4da\"/><circle cx=\"50\" cy=\"29\" r=\"16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#f4c542\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><rect x=\"71\" y=\"12\" width=\"34\" height=\"34\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#1c3a28\"/><circle cx=\"88\" cy=\"29\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#22262b\"/><rect x=\"109\" y=\"12\" width=\"34\" height=\"34\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#1c3a28\"/><circle cx=\"126\" cy=\"29\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#22262b\"/><rect x=\"147\" y=\"12\" width=\"34\" height=\"34\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#1c3a28\"/><circle cx=\"164\" cy=\"29\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#22262b\"/><rect x=\"185\" y=\"12\" width=\"34\" height=\"34\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#1c3a28\"/><circle cx=\"202\" cy=\"29\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#e8e4da\"/><text x=\"140\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#cfe6d8\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"system-ui\">place → every trapped disc between yours flips</text></g></svg>","t":"Place a disc so that one or more straight lines of enemy discs are trapped between your new disc and another of yours — every trapped disc flips to your color, in all directions at once. Every legal move must flip at least one disc; the hints toggle shows them."},{"h":"No move? Pass","t":"If you have no flipping move, your turn is skipped automatically. When NEITHER player can move, the game ends — even with empty squares left."},{"h":"Corners are forever","t":"A corner disc can never be flipped — it anchors entire edges. The squares diagonally next to corners (the X-squares) are poison early: they usually hand the corner away.","ex":"They take an X-square on move 12. You wait, build toward it, and the corner falls into your lap — along with both edges."},{"h":"Fewer is better (early)","t":"Counter-intuitive: a small mid-game disc count is often STRONG — it means your opponent has many discs to flip and few safe moves. Mobility wins the middle; the count only matters at the end."},{"h":"vs Computer","t":"Easy plays loose, Medium fights for mobility, Hard prizes corners and will make you pay for X-squares."}]},"scrabble":{"title":"Scrabble","sections":[{"h":"Goal","t":"Build words crossword-style on the board. When the game ends, the highest total score wins."},{"h":"Setup","t":"Each player draws 7 tiles from the bag of 100. Your rack is hidden behind the pass curtain — only you see it on your turn."},{"h":"Your first word","t":"The very first word of the game must cover the center ★ square and be at least 2 letters long."},{"h":"Playing a word","t":"Tap a rack tile, then tap a board square to place it. All the tiles you play in one turn must sit in a single row or column with no gaps, and the word must connect to tiles already on the board. The score preview turns green when your play is a valid word — red means something's wrong (tap it to see why). Tap Play word to commit.","ex":"CAT is on the board. You add H above the C and S after the T: you've made both CHAT down and CATS across — and you score BOTH words this turn."},{"h":"Premium squares","svg":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 280 74\"><g font-family=\"system-ui\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"8\" width=\"58\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#7db8d8\"/><text x=\"35\" y=\"31\" fill=\"#123\">DL</text><rect x=\"74\" y=\"8\" width=\"58\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#4f9b6e\"/><text x=\"103\" y=\"31\" fill=\"#fff\">TL</text><rect x=\"142\" y=\"8\" width=\"58\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#e0a3b8\"/><text x=\"171\" y=\"31\" fill=\"#5a2038\">DW</text><rect x=\"210\" y=\"8\" width=\"58\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#e08a4f\"/><text x=\"239\" y=\"31\" fill=\"#5a2c10\">TW</text><text x=\"35\" y=\"64\" fill=\"#cfe\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"400\">letter ×2</text><text x=\"103\" y=\"64\" fill=\"#cfe\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"400\">letter ×3</text><text x=\"171\" y=\"64\" fill=\"#cfe\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"400\">word ×2</text><text x=\"239\" y=\"64\" fill=\"#cfe\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"400\">word ×3</text></g></svg>","t":"DL and TL multiply one letter; DW and TW multiply the whole word. A premium only counts the first time a tile is placed on it — after that it's just a normal square. Letter premiums apply before word premiums.","ex":"QUIZ with the Q (10 points) on a TL and the Z (10) on a DW: Q becomes 30, so Q30+U1+I1+Z10 = 42, then the whole word doubles for the DW — 84 points."},{"h":"Blanks","t":"The two blank tiles can be any letter — you choose when you place one — but they're worth 0 points. Choose wisely: a blank stays the letter you picked forever."},{"h":"Bingo!","t":"Play all 7 of your tiles in one turn and you earn a 50-point bonus on top of the word score."},{"h":"Stuck?","t":"Swap trades any number of your tiles for new ones from the bag — that's your whole turn. Pass gives up your turn. If six turns in a row pass with no score, the game ends."},{"h":"Game end","t":"When the bag is empty and one player uses their last tile, the game ends: that player gains the value of everyone's leftover tiles, and everyone else loses the value of their own leftovers. Highest total wins."}]},"shutbox":{"title":"Shut the Box","sections":[{"h":"Goal","t":"Flip down tiles 1–9 to match your dice. Lowest leftover total wins the round — shut them ALL and you've Shut the Box."},{"h":"Your turn","t":"Roll two dice, then flip down any set of OPEN tiles that adds up exactly to the roll. Keep rolling and flipping until no combination of open tiles matches a roll — then your round ends and your score is the sum of what's still open.","ex":"Roll 9 with everything open: flip 9, or 8+1, or 7+2, or 6+3, or 5+4, or 6+2+1… your pick. Flexibility now prevents dead rolls later."},{"h":"One die","t":"Once tiles 7, 8 and 9 are all down, you may roll a single die — the button appears. Small targets, small dice."},{"h":"Strategy","t":"Spend BIG tiles early — they're the hardest to shed and the most expensive to be stuck with. Keep little tiles around for awkward rolls: a lone open 1 and 2 can absorb a 3.","ex":"Roll 8: taking the 8 keeps maximum flexibility; taking 5+3 keeps the dangerous 8 alive. Take the 8."},{"h":"The round","t":"Both players take a full turn from the same fresh box; lower leftover total takes the round. A perfect shut-out ends it in glory — the stats remember every box you shut."}]},"snakes":{"title":"Snakes & Ladders","sections":[{"h":"Goal","t":"Race from square 1 to square 100. Pure luck — youngest player wins exactly as often as anyone, which is the whole charm."},{"h":"Your turn","t":"Roll the die and move that many squares along the winding path. Roll a 6 and you go again."},{"h":"Ladders & snakes","t":"Land exactly at a ladder's FOOT and climb to its top — a free leap forward. Land on a snake's HEAD and you slide all the way down its body. Squares mid-ladder and mid-snake do nothing — only the foot and the head trigger.","ex":"The big ladder near the start can rocket you half the board on turn one. The long snake near 98 has ended dynasties."},{"h":"The finish","t":"Square 100 must be hit EXACTLY. Roll too many and you don't move at all this turn — stuck at 97 rolling 5s while everyone howls."},{"h":"House flavor","t":"It's a racing game with built-in drama — perfect first game for new players, and the snakes hurt the same at any age."}]},"sorry":{"title":"Sorry!","sections":[{"h":"Goal","t":"Race all four of your pawns from Start, clockwise around the board, and into your Home. First player with all four pawns Home wins."},{"h":"Cards, not dice","t":"Draw a card each turn — the card tells you what you may do. If you can't legally do anything the card allows, your turn is over."},{"h":"Getting out","t":"Only a 1 or a 2 moves a pawn out of Start (onto the square just outside). A 2 also lets you draw again after your move — whatever the move was."},{"h":"The cards","t":"1/2: out of Start, or move forward that many. 3/5/8/12: move forward exactly that. 4: move BACKWARD 4. 7: split the move between two pawns (all 7 must be used). 10: forward 10 or backward 1. 11: forward 11, or SWAP places with any opponent pawn. Sorry!: take a pawn from Start and land it right on any opponent pawn — they go back to Start.","ex":"A backward 4 right after leaving Start tucks you just shy of your own Home stretch — the fastest trip in the game. Watch the grown-ups fight for it."},{"h":"Slides","svg":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 280 64\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"22\" width=\"260\" height=\"20\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#1c2b22\"/><polygon points=\"30,32 50,22 50,42\" fill=\"#2f6fd0\"/><rect x=\"50\" y=\"27\" width=\"150\" height=\"10\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#2f6fd0\"/><circle cx=\"215\" cy=\"32\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#d8312b\"/><path d=\"M60 14 H190\" stroke=\"#f4c542\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/><polygon points=\"186,8 198,14 186,20\" fill=\"#f4c542\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"58\" fill=\"#cfe6d8\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"system-ui\">land on the triangle → slide to the end, bumping EVERYONE</text></svg>","t":"Land on the triangle tip of a slide that ISN'T your color and you ride it to the end — bumping every pawn along the way back to Start, theirs or yours!"},{"h":"Bumping & safety","t":"Land exactly on an opponent's pawn and it returns to Start. Your colored Safety Zone near Home is yours alone — opponents can never enter, swap, or Sorry! you there."},{"h":"Home","t":"Pawns enter Home by exact count only. Once Home, a pawn is finished and safe forever."}]},"trouble":{"title":"Trouble","sections":[{"h":"Goal","t":"Race all four of your pegs from your home tray, once around the track, and up your finish lane. First player to get all four pegs into the finish wins."},{"h":"The Pop-O-Matic","t":"Tap the dome in the middle to pop the die — that's your roll. No dice to lose under the couch since 1965."},{"h":"Getting out","t":"Pegs start OFF the board in your corner tray. You need to pop a 6 to bring a peg out onto your starting spot. No 6 and no pegs on the track? Your turn is lost.","ex":"You pop a 4 but all four pegs are still in your tray — nothing can move, turn over. Pop a 6 and a peg comes out AND you pop again!"},{"h":"Pop a 6","t":"Every 6 gives you another pop after you move. Chain them — the celebration sound gets bigger with every 6 in a row."},{"h":"Bumping","svg":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 280 70\"><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"35\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#2f6fd0\"/><circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"35\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#d8312b\"/><path d=\"M62 35 H112\" stroke=\"#f4c542\" stroke-width=\"3\" marker-end=\"url(#a)\"/><defs><marker id=\"a\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z\" fill=\"#f4c542\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M150 28 Q190 0 232 24\" stroke=\"#d8312b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 4\"/><polygon points=\"228,16 238,26 224,28\" fill=\"#d8312b\"/><text x=\"196\" y=\"62\" fill=\"#cfe6d8\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"system-ui\">bumped back to the tray!</text></svg>","t":"Land exactly on an opponent's peg and it gets bumped all the way back to their home tray — they'll need a 6 to come out again. You can never land on your OWN peg."},{"h":"The finish lane","t":"After a full lap, your pegs turn up your colored finish lane. You need the exact count to step into each finish spot — overshooting isn't allowed, so a peg can be stuck waiting for the right roll."},{"h":"🌐 Play online (2 players)","t":"Tap the blue Online button to play across two devices. The first time, choose who plays on this device. One player taps Create a game and shares the 4-letter code; the other taps Join and enters it. When both have joined, the host taps Start. On your turn, pop the die and move; on your opponent's turn the board shows “their turn…” and waits. Both devices need an internet connection.","ex":"Around the same table or across town — same game, just on two phones. Closing the app and rejoining with the same code puts you back in your seat."},{"h":"vs Computer","t":"The vs Computer button lets the computer take the second player's seat: Easy plays loose (great for learning), Medium plays solid priorities, Hard also dodges your likely bumps."}]},"urgame":{"title":"Royal Game of Ur","sections":[{"h":"The oldest game on the shelf","t":"Played in Mesopotamia 4,500 years ago — boards have been dug out of royal tombs. Race all 7 of your pieces along your path and off the far end before your opponent does."},{"h":"The board","svg":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 280 110\"><g><rect x=\"10\" y=\"10\" width=\"260\" height=\"90\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#5a3f24\"/><g font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><rect x=\"18\" y=\"15\" width=\"27\" height=\"23\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#9fb8cb\"/><text x=\"31.5\" y=\"32\" fill=\"#3c3c6e\">✸</text><rect x=\"49\" y=\"15\" width=\"27\" height=\"23\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e9d9b8\"/><rect x=\"80\" y=\"15\" width=\"27\" height=\"23\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e9d9b8\"/><rect x=\"111\" y=\"15\" width=\"27\" height=\"23\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e9d9b8\"/><rect x=\"204\" y=\"15\" width=\"27\" height=\"23\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#9fb8cb\"/><text x=\"217.5\" y=\"32\" fill=\"#3c3c6e\">✸</text><rect x=\"235\" y=\"15\" width=\"27\" height=\"23\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e9d9b8\"/><rect x=\"18\" y=\"42\" width=\"27\" height=\"23\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e9d9b8\"/><rect x=\"49\" y=\"42\" width=\"27\" height=\"23\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e9d9b8\"/><rect x=\"80\" y=\"42\" width=\"27\" height=\"23\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e9d9b8\"/><rect x=\"111\" y=\"42\" width=\"27\" height=\"23\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#9fb8cb\"/><text x=\"124.5\" y=\"59\" fill=\"#3c3c6e\">✸</text><rect x=\"142\" y=\"42\" width=\"27\" height=\"23\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e9d9b8\"/><rect x=\"173\" y=\"42\" width=\"27\" height=\"23\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e9d9b8\"/><rect x=\"204\" y=\"42\" width=\"27\" height=\"23\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e9d9b8\"/><rect x=\"235\" y=\"42\" width=\"27\" height=\"23\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e9d9b8\"/><rect x=\"18\" y=\"69\" width=\"27\" height=\"23\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#9fb8cb\"/><text x=\"31.5\" y=\"86\" fill=\"#3c3c6e\">✸</text><rect x=\"49\" y=\"69\" width=\"27\" height=\"23\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e9d9b8\"/><rect x=\"80\" y=\"69\" width=\"27\" height=\"23\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e9d9b8\"/><rect x=\"111\" y=\"69\" width=\"27\" height=\"23\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e9d9b8\"/><rect x=\"204\" y=\"69\" width=\"27\" height=\"23\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#9fb8cb\"/><text x=\"217.5\" y=\"86\" fill=\"#3c3c6e\">✸</text><rect x=\"235\" y=\"69\" width=\"27\" height=\"23\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e9d9b8\"/></g><text x=\"140\" y=\"55\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#5a3f24\" font-family=\"system-ui\" font-weight=\"700\">← the shared battle lane →</text></g></svg>","t":"Your private lane is the row nearest you; the middle row is the BATTLE LANE you both share. Your path: down your own lane, all the way along the middle, then a short hook home at the far end — 14 squares in all."},{"h":"The dice","t":"Four pyramid dice, each landing marked (1) or unmarked (0). Your roll is the total: 0 to 4. Roll a zero and your whole turn is lost — the table is allowed to laugh."},{"h":"Moving","t":"Move ONE piece exactly your roll: bring a new piece onto your lane, advance a piece on the board, or bear a piece off the end (exact count required — a 3 can't carry a piece 2 squares from home). You can never land on your own piece. No legal move? Turn lost."},{"h":"Battle!","t":"Land on an enemy piece in the shared lane and it's captured — sent all the way back to their starting pool to begin again.","ex":"Their piece sits 3 ahead of yours in the middle lane. Roll a 3, land on it, and it goes home — there are no friendly squares out there… except one."},{"h":"Rosettes ✸","t":"Five flower squares. Land on ANY rosette and you immediately roll again. The center rosette — right in the battle lane — is also a SAFE HAVEN: a piece there can never be captured, and enemies can't land on it while you're parked."},{"h":"Winning","t":"First player to walk all 7 pieces off the far end wins. The score line tracks pieces home: 7 ends it."},{"h":"vs Computer","t":"The computer can take the second seat — Hard knows which battle-lane squares your dice can reach and plays around them."}]},"uttt":{"title":"Ultimate Tic-Tac-Toe","sections":[{"h":"Goal","t":"It's tic-tac-toe made of tic-tac-toes: win three small boards in a row to win the big board."},{"h":"The one rule that matters","svg":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 280 100\"><g stroke=\"#cfe6d8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"20\" y=\"10\" width=\"80\" height=\"80\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"46\" y2=\"90\"/><line x1=\"73\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"73\" y2=\"90\"/><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"36\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"36\"/><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"63\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"63\"/></g><text x=\"85\" y=\"32\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#f4c542\" font-family=\"system-ui\" font-weight=\"800\">X</text><path d=\"M104 28 Q150 0 196 38\" stroke=\"#f4c542\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/><polygon points=\"190,30 200,40 186,42\" fill=\"#f4c542\"/><g stroke=\"#cfe6d8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"180\" y=\"10\" width=\"80\" height=\"80\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><line x1=\"206\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"206\" y2=\"90\"/><line x1=\"233\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"233\" y2=\"90\"/><line x1=\"180\" y1=\"36\" x2=\"260\" y2=\"36\"/><line x1=\"180\" y1=\"63\" x2=\"260\" y2=\"63\"/></g><text x=\"120\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#cfe6d8\" font-family=\"system-ui\">your square → their board</text></svg>","t":"WHERE you play inside a small board decides WHICH small board your opponent must play in next: top-right square sends them to the top-right board, center square to the center board, and so on."},{"h":"Free moves","t":"If you're sent to a board that's already won or full, you may play in ANY open board — a free move, and they're gold. Sometimes the best square is a worse local move that denies your opponent a free move."},{"h":"Thinking two layers","t":"Every move is two decisions in one: a square here, and a destination for them. Winning a small board means nothing if the move that wins it hands your opponent the center board.","ex":"You can take the bottom-left board now — but the winning square sends them to the center board, where they have two in a row. Decline the bait."},{"h":"Winning","t":"Three small boards in a row — across, down, diagonal — takes the game. Drawn small boards count for nobody; if the big board fills with no line, the game is a draw."}]},"war":{"title":"War","sections":[{"h":"Goal","t":"Win ALL the cards. No decisions, no mercy — just fate, flips, and bragging rights."},{"h":"Battle","t":"Each player flips their top card. Higher card takes both — Aces high. Won cards go under your stack."},{"h":"WAR!","t":"A tie means WAR: each player lays THREE cards face-down, then one face-up. The new face-up cards fight — winner takes everything on the table. Tie again? The war grows. The pile gets ridiculous. That's the point.","ex":"Two Kings collide with 9 cards already down — the next flip is suddenly worth 17 cards. The room goes quiet."},{"h":"Running dry","t":"If you can't fund a war — not enough cards to lay down — you lose on the spot. Live by the deck, die by the deck."},{"h":"How long?","t":"Honestly? Anywhere from two minutes to the heat death of the universe. The card counters track the tide — a big war swings everything."}]},"yahtzee":{"title":"Yahtzee","sections":[{"h":"Goal","t":"Thirteen rounds, thirteen scorecard boxes — fill them all and the highest total wins."},{"h":"Your turn","t":"Roll five dice up to THREE times. After each roll, tap dice to hold them (they keep their value) and re-roll the rest. Then you MUST score one open box — even if the best option is a zero."},{"h":"The upper section","t":"Ones through Sixes score the sum of just those dice. Score 63+ up there (an average of three of each number) and you earn a +35 bonus — chasing that bonus quietly decides most close games.","ex":"Three Fives = 15 in the Fives box: exactly on pace for the bonus. Two Fives = 10 means you'll owe the difference somewhere else."},{"h":"The lower section","t":"3 of a Kind and 4 of a Kind score ALL five dice. Full House (3+2) = 25. Small Straight (4 in a row) = 30. Large Straight (5 in a row) = 40. Chance = sum of anything. YAHTZEE — five of a kind — = 50."},{"h":"Extra Yahtzees","t":"Roll a second Yahtzee with the Yahtzee box already scored at 50 and you bank a +100 bonus, then score the dice in another box. If your Yahtzee box holds a zero, no bonus — ouch."},{"h":"Knowing when to zero","t":"Sometimes the play is sacrificing: a dead roll should zero your least-needed box (Ones and Yahtzee are the usual victims), protecting the boxes that score big.","ex":"Final rolls show 2,2,3,4,6 with only Large Straight and Sixes open. Zero the straight — one die of Sixes is worth more than a miracle chase."}]},"onecardleft":{"title":"One Card Left!","sections":[{"h":"Goal","t":"Be the first to empty your hand. Play your very last card and you win the round. Two to four can play, and any empty seat can be taken by the computer."},{"h":"Your turn","svg":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 280 100\"><g font-family=\"system-ui\"><rect x=\"12\" y=\"14\" width=\"44\" height=\"62\" rx=\"7\" fill=\"#fff\"/><rect x=\"17\" y=\"19\" width=\"34\" height=\"52\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#3f86e0\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"53\" font-size=\"26\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">6</text><text x=\"34\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"9.5\" fill=\"#cfe6d8\" text-anchor=\"middle\">on the pile</text><path d=\"M62 45 H78\" stroke=\"#f4c542\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><polygon points=\"76,40 86,45 76,50\" fill=\"#f4c542\"/><rect x=\"92\" y=\"14\" width=\"44\" height=\"62\" rx=\"7\" fill=\"#fff\"/><rect x=\"97\" y=\"19\" width=\"34\" height=\"52\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#3f86e0\"/><text x=\"114\" y=\"53\" font-size=\"26\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">9</text><rect x=\"144\" y=\"14\" width=\"44\" height=\"62\" rx=\"7\" fill=\"#fff\"/><rect x=\"149\" y=\"19\" width=\"34\" height=\"52\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#e5413a\"/><text x=\"166\" y=\"53\" font-size=\"26\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">6</text><rect x=\"196\" y=\"14\" width=\"44\" height=\"62\" rx=\"7\" fill=\"#fff\"/><rect x=\"201\" y=\"19\" width=\"34\" height=\"52\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#2b2b2b\"/><circle cx=\"210\" cy=\"33\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#e5413a\"/><circle cx=\"231\" cy=\"33\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#e3a81f\"/><circle cx=\"210\" cy=\"57\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#3f9a5a\"/><circle cx=\"231\" cy=\"57\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#3f86e0\"/><text x=\"166\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"9.5\" fill=\"#cfe6d8\" text-anchor=\"middle\">any blue · any 6 · or a wild</text></g></svg>","t":"Look at the card on top of the pile, then lay down one card that matches it by COLOR or by NUMBER — the symbol cards match the same way. A wild can be played on anything.","ex":"The pile shows a blue 6. You may play any other blue card, any 6 of any color, or a wild — your choice."},{"h":"Draw if you're stuck","t":"No playable card? Draw from the pile — and keep drawing until you turn one up. You can play that fresh card right away, or tap Keep it to hold it and end your turn."},{"h":"Action cards","svg":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 280 96\"><g font-family=\"system-ui\"><rect x=\"24\" y=\"8\" width=\"56\" height=\"64\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fff\"/><rect x=\"29\" y=\"13\" width=\"46\" height=\"54\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#e5413a\"/><circle cx=\"52\" cy=\"40\" r=\"14\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><line x1=\"42\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"62\" y2=\"50\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text x=\"52\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#cfe6d8\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Skip</text><rect x=\"112\" y=\"8\" width=\"56\" height=\"64\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fff\"/><rect x=\"117\" y=\"13\" width=\"46\" height=\"54\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#3f9a5a\"/><path d=\"M128 34 H150\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.4\"/><polygon points=\"150,29 159,34 150,39\" fill=\"#fff\"/><path d=\"M152 46 H130\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.4\"/><polygon points=\"130,41 121,46 130,51\" fill=\"#fff\"/><text x=\"140\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#cfe6d8\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Reverse</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"8\" width=\"56\" height=\"64\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fff\"/><rect x=\"205\" y=\"13\" width=\"46\" height=\"54\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#3f86e0\"/><text x=\"228\" y=\"49\" font-size=\"25\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+2</text><text x=\"228\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#cfe6d8\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Draw Two</text></g></svg>","t":"Skip jumps the next player's turn entirely. Reverse flips the direction of play around the table — and with just two players it bounces straight back, so you go again. Draw Two makes the next player take two cards AND miss their turn."},{"h":"Wild cards","t":"A Wild lets you name the color that play must follow — drop it whenever you like. A Wild Draw Four does the same and makes the next player draw four and lose their turn. By default a Draw card can't be passed along: when one lands on you, you take the cards. Switch on Stacking before the game and you can answer any Draw card with another Draw card — a +2 or +4 — piling the whole total onto the next player instead.","ex":"Stuck with nothing the pile will take? A Wild switches the whole table over to your strongest color."},{"h":"“One Card Left!”","t":"The instant a player is down to a single card, the table calls it out for them — automatically, with a little chime. No need to remember to announce it, and no penalty if you would have forgotten; it's just the warning bell that someone's about to go out."},{"h":"Passing the device","t":"With more than one person, the screen hides each hand between turns — pass the phone and tap when you're ready, no peeking. Playing solo against the computers? Your hand stays up the whole time and they take their turns on their own."}]}};
